  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 108 AM EDT Mon Sep 28 2026\n\nIn the upper levels, a ridge is over the Great Plains and \nMidwest. A closed low is centered near New Jersey. At the surface,\nhigh pressure is over the Great Lakes extending southward to the \nTennessee Valley. A Nor'easter is just off the coast of New Jersey\ndrifting northward slowly. Dry, sunny weather with pleasant \ntemperatures will continue today with highs mainly in the upper \n70s and lower 80s. \n\nBy Tuesday, the pattern starts to change with a ridge over the \nTennessee and Ohio River Valleys. A closed low over the Southwest is \ndrifting eastward very slowly. At the surface, weak high pressure \nwill be centered near the Carolinas. The system out west weakens \nlate in the week near Texas. A warming trend will become noticeable \nby Tuesday with highs in the 80s for the rest of the workweek \n(around 90 degrees near Chattanooga). Dry weather will continue \nuntil low rain chances return on Friday. \n\nBy Friday, a ridge will be centered near FL/GA/SC as a trough dips \ninto the Ohio Valley. The position of the ridge will supply deep \nlayer moisture from the Gulf. Rain chances start to increase on \nFriday but higher chances are likely on Saturday as a slow moving \ncold front moves into the region. The wet pattern will likely \ncontinue into Sunday but it is still pretty far out and things may \nchange with the pattern.",
